      "id": "f4438b5e-5dfb-411c-8578-8ef862d3216a",
      "identifier": "DIFF-1",
      "title": "Publish reusable Diffpanel packages for native review integrations",
      "url": "https://linear.app/21n/issue/DIFF-1/publish-reusable-diffpanel-packages-for-native-review-integrations",
      "description": "## Summary\n\nPublish Diffpanel's reusable engine and extract shared presentation and generation contracts so Outright can provide native review chapters without copying the implementation.\n\n## Problem and expected outcome\n\nCurrent source separates core, Git capture and storage from the VS Code surface, but all three engine packages are private workspace packages at version 0.0.0. Some reusable presentation logic remains inside the extension. Consumers should install versioned packages and use the same snapshot, coverage, persistence and presentation rules.\n\n## Scope\n\n* Release @diffpanel/core, @diffpanel/git and @diffpanel/storage with explicit package contents, exports, compatibility metadata and tested dependency resolution.\n* Expose browser-safe schemas/validation separately from Node hashing and process/filesystem APIs.\n* Extract chapter navigation, counts, repetitive-change grouping and diagram policy into a shared presentation package; exact package naming is a proposal.\n* Share provider-neutral generation instructions and output contracts between the CLI skill and native consumers.\n* Harden capture with cancellation, time/output/size budgets, safe path and symlink handling, and consistent content/patch capture during concurrent edits.\n* Add bounded run listing, retention/garbage collection and interrupted-write recovery to shared storage.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nOutright UI or provider scheduling; a mandatory shared React library; hosted review services; changes to staging/committing behavior. This issue captures future work, not immediate implementation or publication authorization.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n* A clean external consumer installs released packages without the Diffpanel checkout, workspace links or VS Code.\n* Capture, prepare, validate, publish, reopen and read saved before/after content work through package APIs for worktree, staged, range and repository scopes.\n* Browser imports build without Node-only modules; server imports retain capture and storage functionality.\n* CLI, extension and external consumer share exact-coverage validation and extracted presentation/generation contracts; malformed, missing, duplicate and out-of-scope evidence is rejected.\n* Cancellation terminates owned subprocesses; oversized input/output is bounded; outside-repository symlinks are handled safely; concurrent edits cannot silently mismatch patches and saved blobs.\n* Pagination, retention and restart/failure recovery are tested without deleting blobs referenced by retained reviews.\n* Existing extension/CLI behavior and stored reviews remain compatible or have an explicit migration path.\n\n## Dependencies, risks and open questions\n\nThis package release is the upstream dependency for a separate Outright native-review issue. Risks include SQLite ABI compatibility, schema/version drift, capture races, unbounded process output and orphaned blobs. Open questions: registry/scope ownership and access, initial supported runtime matrix, public API stability policy, precise resource budgets, retention defaults and prompt-contract packaging. Details are proposals until implementation design is approved.\n\n## Related dependency\n\nBlocks [OUT-35](https://linear.app/21n/issue/OUT-35).\n\n## Supporting documents\n\n* [Ideation & Product Rationale — DIFF-1: Publish reusable Diffpanel packages for native review integrations](https://linear.app/21n/document/ideation-and-product-rationale-diff-1-publish-reusable-diffpanel-6ea0b33b853d)\n* [Architecture & Delivery Plan — DIFF-1: Publish reusable Diffpanel packages for native review integrations](https://linear.app/21n/document/architecture-and-delivery-plan-diff-1-publish-reusable-diffpanel-05fa6ead2998)",
