P2: `applyRetention` deletes the selected runs first and then calls `garbageCollectBlobs()` unconditionally, but GC throws when any retained run's manifest is unreadable (its deliberate guard). The run deletions are already committed when that happens, so `prune` reports failure while the deletion is partially applied, and every later `prune`/GC attempt on that library fails the same way (unlike `recover()`, which skips GC via `safeToCollect`). Shield the GC call so a bad retained manifest doesn't brick retention: run it only when all retained manifests are readable, or catch and surface the error without claiming the whole operation failed.

