Issue description
Worktree stabilization validates only captured file content, so a path skipped because of a capture budget or file classification can change during capture and still be accepted as unchanged. This can leave a now-reviewable change absent from the immutable review manifest.

Fix Focus Areas
- packages/git/src/capture.ts[172-197]
- packages/git/src/capture.ts[200-223]

Recommended Fix
Retain enough snapshot state for every discovered path, including skipped paths, to detect content, eligibility, and metadata changes during verification. Treat a changed skipped path as an unstable snapshot and rerun capture so the final manifest and skipped-path list are derived from the same worktree state.
```

