P2: `npm publish` without `--tag` attaches the published version to the `latest` dist-tag even when the version is a prerelease (npm docs: "Publishing a package sets the `latest` tag to the published version unless the `--tag` option is used"). Because `resolve-release-tag.mjs` explicitly accepts prerelease tags like `diffpanel-v0.0.3-beta.1`, publishing one would move `latest` to the prerelease — breaking unpinned consumers and blocking the later stable publish with "a newer 'latest' version is already published". Pass `--tag next` (or refuse prerelease tags) for prerelease versions.

