2\. A second client can erase active runs <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code>

<pre>
<b><i>recover</i></b> treats every run directory absent from its current database snapshot as orphaned and also
recursively removes every temporary file without checking for another live writer. Because
<b><i>createPreparedRun</i></b> creates and writes its directory before its database transaction and every
<b><i>open</i></b> invokes recovery, a concurrent client can remove an in-progress run directory or atomic-write
file and make creation fail.
</pre>


<details>
<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>

```
## Issue description
Startup recovery can mistake files and directories belonging to another active store process for interrupted writes and delete them.

## Fix Focus Areas
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[72-79]
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[86-197]
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[369-386]
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[592-602]

## Recommended Fix
Serialize recovery and write operations using a cross-process lock, or record pending runs and temporary writes in SQLite before creating them. Recovery should only delete artifacts proven stale, such as unowned entries older than a safe threshold, rather than every currently unregistered directory or temporary file.
```

