## Reviewer's Guide

This PR converts Diffpanel’s internal modules into five reusable, publishable packages, migrates existing consumers to shared contracts, hardens Git capture and durable storage behavior, and introduces validated tag-driven npm/VSIX release tooling without creating releases or tags.

#### Sequence diagram for bounded Git capture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    User->>CLI: captureReview(request, options)
    CLI->>Git: captureReview(request, limits, signal)
    Git->>Git: runProcess(git, processOptions)
    Git->>Git: readWorktreeContent(filePath)
    Git->>Git: worktreeSnapshotMatches(...)
    alt snapshot changed
        Git->>Git: captureReview(request, retry)
    else snapshot stable
        Git-->>CLI: CapturedReview
    end
    CLI->>Storage: createPreparedRun(captured)
    Storage-->>CLI: PreparedRunReceipt
```

#### Sequence diagram for tagged package publishing

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Maintainer
    Maintainer->>GitHub: Push package-v<version> tag
    GitHub->>Workflow: publish-tag.yml
    Workflow->>Workflow: resolve-release-tag.mjs(tag)
    Workflow->>Package: npm install
    Workflow->>Package: npm run build
    Workflow->>Package: npm test
    Workflow->>Package: npm pack
    Workflow->>Consumer: npm install(tarball)
    Consumer-->>Workflow: Import verification passed
    Workflow->>NPM: npm publish(tarball)
    NPM-->>Workflow: Published package
```

#### Flow diagram for durable storage lifecycle

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Capture["CapturedReview"] --> Prepare["createPreparedRun"]
    Prepare --> Blobs["Content-addressed blobs"]
    Prepare --> Manifest["Immutable manifest"]
    Manifest --> Publish["publish"]
    Publish --> Ready["Ready run"]
    Ready --> List["listRunsPage"]
    Ready --> Content["getFileContent"]
    Ready --> Retention["applyRetention"]
    Retention --> GC["garbageCollectBlobs"]
    Open["DiffpanelStore.open"] --> Recovery["recover"]
    Recovery --> Ready
    Recovery --> Failed["Failed run / recovery report"]
```

