1\. Concurrent clients can lose run content <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code>

<pre>
<b><i>garbageCollectBlobs</i></b> builds its retained set only from committed <b><i>run_blobs</i></b> rows and unlinks every
other valid blob file. <b><i>createPreparedRun</i></b> writes blobs before inserting those references, while
every store open invokes recovery garbage collection, so a concurrent client can delete content
before the new run commits and leave that run referencing missing blobs.
</pre>


