```
## Issue description
Recovery marks runs failed when immutable blobs are missing, but only checks the existence of referenced blob paths and does not detect content corrupted in place. This leaves affected prepared or ready runs reported as healthy until later file-content access performs integrity validation.

## Fix Focus Areas
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[297-305]
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[388-425]
- packages/storage/src/store.ts[464-469]

## Recommended Fix
During recovery, read each distinct manifest-referenced blob, compute its SHA-256 digest, and compare it with the manifest hash. Throw when content is missing or mismatched so the existing recovery path marks every affected referencing run failed, while avoiding duplicate reads for blobs shared by multiple runs through a bounded cache of verified hashes if needed.
```

