**Coordinate maintenance with active filesystem writes.**

Two store instances can operate on the same home concurrently. `garbageCollectBlobs()` can delete a blob after `putBlob()` writes it but before Line 194 records its reference. Recovery can also remove a new run directory before the run transaction commits, or remove an active temporary file before `atomicWrite()` renames it.

These races can make a write fail or commit a run whose files are missing. Use a home-scoped cross-process lock for write, recovery, retention, and garbage-collection operations. Alternatively, persist a staged record before creating files and exclude staged resources from cleanup.






