P2: Spawning `vsce.cmd` without `shell: true` fails on Windows with `EINVAL`: since the CVE-2024-27980 patch (Node 18.20.2/20.12.2/22.0.0+, and this project requires Node >= 22.13), `child_process.spawn` no longer auto-invokes `.cmd`/`.bat` files via `cmd.exe` and throws an error instead. The script explicitly adds a Windows branch (`.cmd` suffix), so Windows packaging is intended but currently broken; the `error` event rejects the promise and the `package` script aborts. Pass `shell: true` when spawning on win32.

