P2: `git write-tree` fails (exit 128, "error building trees") whenever the index contains unmerged entries from a merge conflict, so a staged capture now throws `git write-tree failed ...` instead of capturing anything. The previous implementation used `git diff --cached <base>`, which works in that state, and `mapStatus` still maps `U` to `"unmerged"`, so conflicted staged captures were an intended case. Fall back to the already-coded `--cached` path (the `else` branches of `listChangedPaths`/`readPatch`/`readAfterContent`) when `write-tree` fails, so conflicted indexes degrade gracefully instead of aborting.

